========================================================================
5. A common mistake: pivot() without the list of values
========================================================================
+-------+----+----+----+----+
|product|   2|   3|   4|   5|
+-------+----+----+----+----+
|grinder|NULL|   1|   1|   2|
| kettle|   1|NULL|   2|NULL|
|    mug|NULL|NULL|NULL|   1|
+-------+----+----+----+----+

1. The 1-star column is gone: no one gave 1 star, so Spark never saw
   the value 1. The shape of the report depends on the data.
2. Empty cells are NULL, not 0: the page would print '2 stars | NULL'.
A rating box ALWAYS has 5 bars (the RDD version's 5-counter zeroValue).
Say it in the code: list the values, or use count(when(...)) as above.
